**Finding: Compliant** (no redline proposed).

The agreement meets the playbook's **preferred** position on EXCLUSIVITY. Clause 1 (Kubient Services) contains an express anti-exclusivity carve-out: "Nothing herein is intended nor shall be construed as creating an exclusive arrangement between Customer and Kubient. This Agreement will not restrict Customer offering Inventory via other agents or otherwise selling Inventory to any third parties."

A full-document sweep for "exclusive", "sole", "requirements", routing language, and third-party restrictions surfaced no obligation binding AP's supply freedom. The other "exclusive"/"sole" hits are unrelated or run in our favour:
- p0002 — non-exclusive license granted *to* AP;
- p0064 — exclusive jurisdiction (forum, not dealing);
- p0065 — each party's own trademarks;
- p0073 — no third-party beneficiaries.

No exclusivity granted to AP exists that would need preserving, and nothing requires narrowing to the fallback.
